MT-JailBench's CoA implementation is itself adapted from YancyKahn/CoA
(Chain of Attack; https://github.com/YancyKahn/CoA). The technique is credited
to its original authors.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled material (vendored byte-for-byte; sha256-pinned in _vendor/SHA256SUMS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- src/mtjb_coa_optimizer/_vendor/mtjb/engine/attacks/coa/prompts.yaml
    CoA attacker chain / prompt-update / binary-judge prompt templates.
- src/mtjb_coa_optimizer/_vendor/mtjb/engine/attacks/coa/similarity_scorer.py
    Holds the LLM-approximation similarity-scoring prompt (SIM_APPROX_PROMPT),
    read verbatim; the surrounding scorer logic is reimplemented in this module.

The CoA control flow and prompt-generation logic are reimplemented from scratch
in src/mtjb_coa_optimizer/ (original to this module, MIT); the method is
credited to its authors. No prompt/dataset body is reproduced in authored code.

